WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.360
Ignorance does not equal shamelessness.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:13.990
It merely reflects purity.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.990
Until the time comes, it's best that we remain pure.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:10.810
Is that you, Hotori?

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.060
How'd you know?

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.180
You put your hand over your mouth and stumbled backwards.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.520
You can see that too?

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.900
My guardian spirit taught me how.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.240
Shizuka-neechan, when did you become a psychic!?

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.490
Gotcha!

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:30.830
Oh, a mirror.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.840
You were watching me through that.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.980
Can't even see through such an elementary trick.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.840
You require more training before you can become an apprentice, lass.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.510
I came to shop for Tattsun's birthday present today.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.330
At an antiques store, of all places.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.690
Oh, maybe this scale...

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:03.160
I've measured the perfect amount of sugar for your coffee!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.870
Yeah, I bet she'd love that!

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.740
Kinda pricey though.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.630
Hey Shizuka-san, would this be good?

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.930
That's kind of hard to say.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.620
Let's see, I think it's...

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.680
Well? You buying it or what?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.350
You still want full price for that!?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:30.540
Oh yeah, kinda off-topic, but I went to Africa recently.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.060
I see. So that explains your weird clothes.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.350
Here. I brought you a souvenir.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.850
Yay! Oh, happy day!

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.240
What the heck is this!?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.220
Creepy! Weird! Unnerving!

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.190
A trinity of freakiness!

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:51.200
Those all mean pretty much the same thing.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:59.080
Basically, it was a gift forced upon me at a wealthy local's wedding ceremony.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:03.980
But he told me that this mask grants the power to locate anyone and anything...

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.210
Whoa... I so don't want this...

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:07.810
Now, now.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.180
Just think of it as a love charm.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.560
Stop it!

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.390
Oh, I just thought of a present for Tattchan.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.990
Her name's Tatt<i>sun</i>.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:22.680
A real cute one, 'kay?

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.900
Happy trails!

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:29.820
I can't help but think she's just conning me into buying her junk.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.330
Good heavens!

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.320
Actually, mice don't really like cheese that much.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.070
It's two days early, but...

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.460
Happy birthday!

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.310
Thanks, everyone.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:46.580
I haven't had a partly like this since grade school.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:51.080
This is from my family.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.480
We call it our seafood salad.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.730
Thank you! I'll treasure it forever!

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.980
I'd rather you eat if while it's still fresh, though.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.650
So you're saying that this is a Sanada Scat Salad.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.070
Too much rhyme, that's a crime.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:12.650
That's the last thing I'd expect you to complain about.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.000
Okay, what else...

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.830
A crate of veggies from the grocery store.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.790
Two free cleaning coupons from the cleaners.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.660
A free bottle of every drink from the 100 yen shop.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:25.920
I bought you a cake. Accept it with gratitude.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.190
T-Thank you...

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:29.480
Now that the party's in full swing,

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.170
it's time for the main event!

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.040
We <i>just</i> started.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.590
The main event is Tatsuno's party, remember?

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.840
Nice segway, MC.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.690
Hang in there!

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.150
Here! A gift from me to you.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:51.370
Thank you.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.880
A beat-up old box?

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.000
There's something inside.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:58.860
Oh, I get it.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.240
I'm supposed to wait until my actual birthday to open it, right?

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.180
Sorry, but that birthday wish won't be coming true.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.010
Huh?

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.510
The key's missing.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:14.100
When I bought it from Kameido Antiques, the lady said it didn't have a key when she first got it.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.020
What?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.520
But that's what makes it so romantic!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.030
Those long, autumn nights, thinking about what could be inside...

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.150
...isn't that just enchanting?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.320
She said I could pass it off if I fed her that.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.320
No way! It's kinda creeping me out.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.320
Josephine Joestar, Jojo! I've always wanted to say that.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.820
Man, that was fun!

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.990
We should have parties more often!

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:40.790
This place is pretty much eternally reserved, anyway.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.500
When's your birthday, Sanada?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.580
February.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.710
That was forever ago! Thanks for nothing!

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:49.930
What about you, Granny?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.010
April.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.000
Senpai?

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.110
It's, uh, not really important.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.370
Huh? How come?

00:06:56.370 --> 00:07:01.650
C'mon, don't be shy! Seaside will throw you a huge party!

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.600
Well when's your birthday?

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.390
Mine's in May.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.700
Girls born in May are blessed with wisdom and intellect!

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.940
I could do without your "wisdom" for the rest of my life.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.450
So, when is it, Senpai?

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.660
Speaking of May...

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.120
She's changing the subject.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.120
Ta-da! I found Senpai's student ID.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.870
Don't do it! The consequences of asking are dire!

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:29.260
Let's see...

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.630
September 8th!

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:32.250
That's today!

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.850
Well, I guess that's why she didn't want me to say it.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.810
Look what you did, you little jerk!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.560
You killed the mood, now what?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.140
You better fix this.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.620
Happy birthday!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:10.050
Uh, happy birthday to you.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.720
Oh yeah, you need a present!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.720
I'll run to the candy store real quick!

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.890
Enough with the pity party!

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.890
If you keep picking at it, it'll tear off.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:24.970
The only thing left that I could give was that love charm.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:28.450
Oh? I would've rather got that.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.680
Instead of this Pandora's Box.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:37.700
Okay, if I give Kon the romantic box, and Tattsun the love charm...

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.260
Yeah, that'll work out perfectly!

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:44.360
Why don’t we fix the mood here first?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:48.130
We'll throw you a real party next year, Senpai.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.740
‘Cause now I've memorized your birthday!

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:53.620
September 8th. Kon Futaba's birthday!

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.960
A mortifying memory, Kon Futaba.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.030
Now, none of us will forget.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.970
Don't make it into a stupid poem!

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:04.970
Cup noodles are best if you cook them 45 seconds less than suggested.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:10.620
Oh, I got it!

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:12.870
Wow, awesome! You could be a thief!

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.360
...and be apprehended by me!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:19.230
Maybe if I went senile, you could!

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:24.180
Now then, what's in the box?

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.700
Charms?

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.410
Aw man, that's boring!

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.920
Hey, this is a love charm!

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.930
Guess Tatsuno should have stuck with this instead.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.440
Now that we opened it, it's kinda sad.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.800
Pandora's Box became an ordinary dirty old box.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:50.270
They're coming outta the god damn walls!

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:56.340
How is that a love charm!?

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:59.830
Why would I care about marrying a rich guy from Africa?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.790
Excuse me!

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:09.830
Ah, yes. You're Hotori's friend, Tattchan, right?

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.970
No, I'm Tattsun.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:12.210
I mean, Tatsuno.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:16.220
I've been told that you buy old knicknacks here.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.350
I sure do.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:19.480
I'll just have take a peek and...

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:32.360
Your assignment is to create and upload a functional website.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:36.080
Hey, is "upload" the same thing as "uphill"?

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:39.200
God, just shut up! At least try to help a little.

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:43.590
I'll work on the tags, so you focus on the material.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:44.860
Thanks, Suzuki.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:50.690
Man, I wish I could have been with Suzuki! Why'd I get stuck with the dumbass jock?

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:53.870
'Bout the only thing I'm good for is lifting weights!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:59.120
You don't have to be so serious about it.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.310
Just wing it and throw together something simple.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.290
Finally, I got the title up.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:10.380
I wanna get this page up and running so we can attract customers.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:12.480
Oh, nice! Making an advertisement for our project.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.070
That's like two birds with one stone!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.060
Arashiyama.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:20.400
Here's the drawing you asked for.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.810
Wow, thanks! This is perfect!

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:26.580
Okay, here's the Tattsun Maid pictures I promised you.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:29.070
Marvelous!

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:34.370
I'm gonna put this drawing up on the site.

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:37.020
You'll get busted for false advertising.

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:40.490
You're the one who said to just do whatever.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.710
Well, I guess we'll have to rethink our plan.

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.810
Dismissed. You're to turn in your assignments in two weeks.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.800
Ahh! I didn't even get anything done yet!

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:54.800
Maruko's skies have the best view of the moon.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.780
Thanks for waiting.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:02.380
Okay, who had the curry again?

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:05.140
Ah well, you can just share.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.860
You're horrible! You're even worse than a normal waitress!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:13.120
And she just has to remind me about it while I'm sneaking off from work.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.890
She's starting to act like a cranky old lady.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:20.010
That group offense warrants extra salads and coffee.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.670
Kobuhei, you dumbass!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.010
Don't hurt the poor maid's feelings!

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:26.910
Hey, Tattsuntsun!

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:29.260
My nickname just got even more unpleasant.

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:32.270
Do you have a compyooter at your house?

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.770
Yeah, but mostly for my brother to play his games.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:38.860
How about we work on our project after work?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.150
Well, the thing is...

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.100
Kon-senpai's got a fever, so she's sick in bed.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:47.620
She lives alone, so I thought I'd go and take care of her.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.550
Impossible! I thought they said idiots can't catch colds.

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:52.830
Of all the times to get sick...

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.880
I don't think I've ever caught a cold.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.700
'Cept that time I stayed home in middle school, anyway.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:03.250
You always bragged about never missing school!

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.470
Yeah, you had perfect attendance.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.470
I doubt these guys would ever catch a cold.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.930
Hey, is Sanada home right now?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.020
Oh, Hiroyuki?

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.830
Yeah, he got back a while ago.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:14.480
Perfect.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.310
So there you have it.

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:20.190
Can I go work on my project at
second-choice-Sanada's house?

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:23.790
There I have what? You're still on the clock!

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:25.820
But it's for the advertising too.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.920
Well, we don't have any customers now, anyway. Guess you can go.

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:30.630
Yippie!

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:31.830
There's four of 'em right here!

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:36.750
Oh, you guys are here everyday so I just thought we had weird-shaped furniture.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.150
She's horrible!

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:40.430
The hag's 100 times worse!

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:41.520
She's in a whole ‘nother league.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.880
Those words cut like a knife!

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.560
W-Wait! You're going to Sanada-kun's house?

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.390
Since he's got a computer too.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.770
You can go too.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.370
Hey, wait up!

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.920
Huh? Weren't you going to check on Kon-senpai?

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.270
We can go together later.

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:10.310
My PC? Yeah, no problem.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:11.180
When?

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:13.080
Now!?

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.820
We'll pick you up a little something.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:16.750
How about potato croquettes?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.080
Since we're right here by the butcher's.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.080
The butcher's!?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.830
If they buy something that simple, they'll be here in just a few minutes!

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:25.090
And those are the cheapest things they have too!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:28.590
Hey, could you get me some cream puffs from Romand?

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:31.440
What? All right, fine.

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:33.730
Since when have you been Mr. Gourmet?

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.600
You selfish little turd!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.350
All right! That gained me 20 minutes!

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.280
Ah! Oh, crap!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.530
I've got all those nude mags under my desk!

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.450
Excuse us!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.260
Whew! Made it!

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.930
I forgot the most important thing!

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.120
All that downloaded porn is still on there!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.450
Hey, what's this folder for?

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:06.210
Sanada-kun, you creeper!

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.210
It could happen!

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.970
My only choice is to delete all the files!

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.470
I don't even have to think about it!

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:17.220
Hey, we're here!

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:18.510
Hey.

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:21.160
Hey Sanada, you look kinda worn out.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:24.610
Feels like I just suppressed my dark side to become a Jedi.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.380
What're you talking about?

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.110
Here's your cream puffs.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.860
Sorry to barge in like this.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.780
Hey, no problem.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:36.870
So anyway, I wanna put this picture on our front page.

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:41.420
I don't have a scanner, so no can do.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:45.890
Scanners? I thought you were training to be a Jedi.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.550
Anyway, that's not what I was asking about.

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:52.430
A scanner's a machine that scans and digitizes documents onto your computer.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:55.720
Huh? Can't you do anything if you have a computer?

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.400
Ugh, that sounds like something a
computer-illiterate geezer would say.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.050
Well, this was pointless then!

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:00.930
C'mon four eyes, we're leaving!

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.190
Four-eyes?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.440
So I deleted all that for nothing!?

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:08.730
Hey, isn't that the novel I lent you?

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:11.070
Just shoving it up there...

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.530
I'm taking it back with me.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:16.030
NOOO! DON'T LOOK THERE!

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:24.390
Oh, oh god...

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:33.200
See? You can dress it up all you want, but a turd is a turd.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:37.010
Disgusting! From now on, I'll call him Sanada Hustleryuki.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:41.890
It'd be much weirder for a boy his age not to have those lying around.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:46.140
Come on, let's go feed Kon-senpai and go home.

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:50.160
"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama" is a palindrome.

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:56.830
KON DENSUKE!?

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.050
I knew he was a man!

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.200
Men are scary. Men are the devil!

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:06.070
She's a girl living alone, so she used her dad's nameplate.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.090
Maybe she's asleep.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:14.580
It's unlocked.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:16.670
Wow, pretty careless.

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:19.100
Senpai? We're coming in!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.580
Careless! Careless!

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:23.420
C-c-c-c-c-careless...

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:25.810
...less go! That was awesome, Tattsun!

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.490
Keep it down.

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:28.800
You're in a sick person's home!

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.820
But you started it...

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:39.200
That's a wicked fever.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.180
Senpai? Are you okay?

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:45.210
It's a lot worse than I thought.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:48.050
Go air out the futon. I'll make her an ice pack.

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:48.670
Got it!

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:52.670
That guy looks just like the guy who runs the cleaners.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:59.260
When she's calm and sleeping like that, she's actually kinda cute.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.750
It hurts... I'm gonna die, mommy.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.270
Mommy?

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:10.980
Senpai!

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.230
You need to rest!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.220
No choice but to kill you two.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.780
Calm down!, Senpai!

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:21.600
Hey, watch it!

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.790
You were just mumbling in your sleep!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.080
It was just gibberish!

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:31.630
Really?

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:32.840
Dead serious!

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:34.340
Oh, okay.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.830
Okay, Senpai. Just get some rest.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.860
Oh, thanks guys.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.440
I'll be fine on my own if I just get some sleep.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.350
Whatever you say.

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:48.340
Hotori fell from a desk too.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:52.090
Looks like your temperature's gone down from all that sweating.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:57.110
I'm gonna go cook something, so behave yourself.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:58.610
What'cha making?

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:00.490
Leek and egg rice gruel.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.640
That sounds kinda yummy.

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:06.980
Fine. I'll just eat those cream puffs then.

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.110
Huh? They're not here!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.380
Of course they aren't. You gave them to Sanada-kun.

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:16.990
Shoot. I gave them to Hustleryuki for nothing!

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:24.250
In memory of Sanada. For his playboys were found by two girls today.

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:27.250
Today's cream puffs are kind of bitter.

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:33.620
She's got enough CDs to open a store.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:36.040
She really loves music.

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:38.220
Whoa! A GITAH!

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.240
Looks like the strings are kinda fat and a few are missing.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.560
Is this a beginner's guitar?

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:45.240
It's a bass.

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:49.120
You're an inch away from getting decked by every bassist in the world.

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.600
Oh, so this is a bass, huh?

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:56.090
Hmm? There's no music coming out!

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:58.990
God, you're a pest!

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.010
Look, the amp's not even switched on.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.000
So the music comes from that huge speaker?

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.530
W-What's going on?

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.850
Nothing at all!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:24.030
Okay, let's just go back to bed, 'kay?

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:27.520
You're the one who flipped the switch!

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:31.460
We're back!

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:32.790
Sorry we're late!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.780
Hey, welcome back.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:35.690
Hey there!

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:38.730
Hey! You ditching work again?

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:41.950
Granny aside, I'm worried about this store!

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:45.030
I went and came back, okay?

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:48.050
Hiroyuki seems kinda depressed. Something happen?

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:53.560
Y-Your son, Hustleryuki has lecherous tendencies.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:55.470
Why that little...!

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:57.010
Did he do something to you, Hotori-chan?

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:58.760
Over my dead body!

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.030
You sure? You sure you're okay?

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:05.030
Today's been a total bust.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:13.150
Tattsun's staying home today.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:16.320
I wonder if she caught Senpai's cold?

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:19.760
Speaking of which, my dad's been feeling crummy since last night.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:22.970
Must be a virus going around.

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:25.760
I don't feel too hot either. I think I'll go home and sleep.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:30.710
Huh?

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:34.840
Granny, what's wrong?

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.600
Oh, Hotori?

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:40.470
First time in ages that I've caught a cold.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:44.490
It's nothing serious, but I don't want you catching it, so go on home, dear.

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:49.490
It's spreading at an alarming rate...

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:51.870
I better be careful too.

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:53.850
Idiots can't catch colds.

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:01.130
Oh dear, I must have a cold!

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:09.120
I'm so healthy it makes me sick!

00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:10.970
What should I do?

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:45.240
And so they took flight, vanishing without a trace.

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:47.980
Eloping... how romantic!

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:51.720
Sounds like that geezer was quite the delinquent as a kid.

00:23:51.720 --> 00:23:53.220
No, he wasn't a troublemaker.

00:23:53.220 --> 00:23:58.600
I meant flight, as in flying off in an airplane.

00:23:58.600 --> 00:24:01.300
Really? Then what if they escaped by sea?

00:24:01.300 --> 00:24:02.890
Eswimming, I guess?

00:24:02.890 --> 00:24:04.880
How is that even possible?

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:08.380
Next time: 7th Street: Lovers' Midnight Dash

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.810
‘Keeps on turning lazily.
